WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.440
Speaker 1: The state of Arkansas continues to&nbsp;
waste the time and resources of the people in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:16.380
the state now by restricting school bathroom&nbsp;
use by transgender people under the leadership,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.380 --> 00:00:23.040
if you can call it that, of Republican Governor&nbsp;
Sarah Huckabee Sanders. They have banned CRT from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:28.860
schools, which wasn't being taught in schools, and&nbsp;
they are generally wasting a ton of time. And now&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.860 --> 00:00:35.580
the news is, yes, indeed, Governor Sarah Huckabee&nbsp;
Sanders signed a new law prohibiting trans people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.580 --> 00:00:42.660
at public schools from using the restroom of their&nbsp;
choice. This would make Arkansas the fourth place&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.660 --> 00:00:49.860
to put such restrictions on public schools. And&nbsp;
it requires that those that individuals use the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.860 --> 00:00:58.440
bathroom that match, I believe the wording they're&nbsp;
using is their birth sex. Alabama, Oklahoma and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.440 --> 00:01:05.160
Tennessee have filed similar restrictions,&nbsp;
although lawsuits have been filed. And this is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.160 --> 00:01:11.280
something that is growing and growing and growing.&nbsp;
Here is where I want to focus today on this issue.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.280 --> 00:01:18.900
It's really important to talk about the absurdity&nbsp;
of the bathroom issue. There is simply no evidence&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.900 --> 00:01:25.560
that trans people in public bathrooms pose a&nbsp;
threat to the safety of others, whether we're&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.560 --> 00:01:30.960
talking about kids, adults in schools, out at&nbsp;
restaurants, in malls, or whatever the case may&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.960 --> 00:01:37.260
be. One of the big arguments, really, the biggest&nbsp;
argument that the right makes is that if anybody&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.260 --> 00:01:43.920
can just use whatever bathroom they want based&nbsp;
on their alleged their stated gender identity,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.640 --> 00:01:51.060
it opens the door to stalking and sexual assault&nbsp;
and pedophilia and all sorts of different things.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.060 --> 00:01:56.820
There is absolutely no evidence that that is the&nbsp;
case. And in fact, when you look at the data,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.820 --> 00:02:03.300
there are widespread studies about this. Studies&nbsp;
have shown that trans people are way more likely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.300 --> 00:02:09.720
to be the victims of violence and the victims of&nbsp;
harassment in public restrooms than they are to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.720 --> 00:02:18.660
the perpetrators. There's a 2013 study from UCLA&nbsp;
School of Law. It finds 70% of trans respondents&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.660 --> 00:02:25.200
were verbally harassed or assaulted or mistreated&nbsp;
in public restrooms. A 2016 report by the Human&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:32.280
Rights Campaign found that 59% of trans people&nbsp;
avoided using public restrooms in the preceding&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.280 --> 00:02:38.160
year because they were afraid of those negative&nbsp;
experiences. And there's a 2018 study from the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.160 --> 00:02:44.640
AARP, the American Academy of Pediatrics, which&nbsp;
finds trans people and gender nonconforming youth&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.640 --> 00:02:50.940
are more likely to experience verbal and physical&nbsp;
abuse in school restrooms. On the other side of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.940 --> 00:02:59.280
this, there is absolutely no study that finds&nbsp;
that when you look at incidents of harassment,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:06.000
sexual assault, etc., in public bathrooms,&nbsp;
that trans people are overrepresented&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:11.520
relative to their population. There is&nbsp;
just no data that can support that cause.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.240 --> 00:03:17.280
And then there's the last aspect to this. If&nbsp;
your concern is sexual assault or harassment or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.280 --> 00:03:22.500
whatever the case may be, it is already illegal.&nbsp;
It doesn't your gender identity doesn't matter,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.500 --> 00:03:29.460
your genitalia doesn't matter. It is already&nbsp;
illegal to engage in sexual assault or harassment&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.460 --> 00:03:33.660
or stalking or photography or whatever the&nbsp;
case may be in public restrooms. Doesn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.660 --> 00:03:38.640
matter which bathroom you're in. The gender&nbsp;
identity of the individuals involved also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.640 --> 00:03:44.580
doesn't matter. And the law is applied equally.&nbsp;
Whether you are cis, gender or transgender. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.580 --> 00:03:50.220
law is already there and there is no evidence&nbsp;
that trans people are more likely to commit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.820 --> 00:03:58.980
sexual assault or harassment than cisgender&nbsp;
people. So the entire framework here is a moral&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.980 --> 00:04:04.200
panic and fear framework. As is often the case&nbsp;
with right wingers, they don't have the facts&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.200 --> 00:04:09.960
on their side because the facts aren't on their&nbsp;
side. And so it's based. On fear. And the idea,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.960 --> 00:04:15.840
quite frankly, the idea that they want to tell&nbsp;
you is that Hulk Hogan is going to put on a wig,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.840 --> 00:04:24.300
go into a public bathroom and harass little&nbsp;
girls. That's the idea. The image that these&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.300 --> 00:04:29.760
folks want you to believe, it's not happening.&nbsp;
There is no data that backs this up as an actual&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:29.760 --> 00:04:36.540
danger. And Sarah Huckabee Sanders just continues&nbsp;
wasting time on this complete and utter nonsense.

